  "id": "pathological-gambling",
  "term": "pathological gambling",
  "definition": "Pathological gambling is a behavioral disorder marked by intense preoccupation with gambling and the excitement of taking bigger risks. The person cannot reduce or stop gambling even when it leads to serious harm such as lying, stealing, or major losses in relationships, work, or education.",
